/*
updateUIDGID
------------

On Linux, when you specify `containerUser` or `remoteUser`, the container
automatically updates that user’s UID and GID to match your local user.
This prevents permission issues with bind-mounted files.
Default: **true**.

If you already have host files that rely on fixed UID/GID values and must be
accessible from the container, consider turning this feature off to keep the
container user’s IDs unchanged.

Check the current IDs and file ownership inside the container with:

  id      # shows your UID and GID
  ls -l   # shows ownership of files
*/
{
  "name": "1_7-spec_updateRemoteUserUID",
  "build": {
    "dockerfile": "./Dockerfile"
  },
  "containerUser": "root",
  "updateRemoteUserUID": false
}
